 "title": "HTML DOM API",
 "blocks": [
  {
   "type": "h1",
   "text": "HTML DOM API"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Application Programming Interface"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The DOM API (Application Programming Interface) is a set of Methods and Properties\nthat allow JavaScript to change the content, structure, and style of any HTML elements."
  },
  {
   "type": "image",
   "src": "https://www.w3schools.com/img_htmltree_800.svg",
   "alt": "DOM HTML tree"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "html",
   "text": "<html>\n\n<body>\n\n<p id=\"demo\"></p>\n\n<script>\n\n// Access a paragraph Element\n\nconst myPara = document.getElementById(\"demo\");\n\n// Change the content of the Element\n\nmyPara.innerHTML = \"Hello World!\";\n\n</script>\n\n</body>\n\n</html>",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_dom_method"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Example Explained"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "document is the HTML document."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "getElementById() is a document method."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "myPara = getElementById(\"demo\") retrieves the \"demo\" element."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "innerHTML is an element property."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "myPara.innerHTML = \"Hello World!\" changes the property."
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "HTML DOM API Abilities"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The DOM API provides us with the ability to:"
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "ordered": false,
   "items": [
    "Find and select elements",
    "Change element content and attributes",
    "Add, remove, or modify elements",
    "Change CSS styles",
    "Add event listeners to react to user input"
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "JavaScript is the Language"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The DOM API is a standard for how to get, change, add, or delete HTML DOM elements."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "JavaScript is the language used in browsers to access the DOM through the API."
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "API Methods and Properties"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Developers use global objects like document and window as entry points to any API."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "If you want to access any element in an HTML page, you always start with accessing the\ndocument object. The document object represents your web page."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "To manipulate HTML with JavaScript, you first need to select an element."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Below are some examples of how you can use the document object to access HTML:"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Selecting HTML Elements"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Method",
    "Description"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "document.getElementById(id)",
     "Find an element by element id"
    ],
    [
     "document.getElementsByTagName(name)",
     "Find elements by tag name"
    ],
    [
     "document.getElementsByClassName(name)",
     "Find elements by class name"
    ],
    [
     "document.querySelector(selector)",
     "Find the first element that matches a CSS selector"
    ],
    [
     "document.querySelectorAll(selector)",
     "Find all elements that match a CSS selector"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The document object is the owner of all other objects in your web page."
  },
  {
